 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "gas hob keeps clickin on its own since i cleand it, stops then starts agen. drivin me mad. pls help"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I can certainly help you with that uncommanded clicking on your gas hob. Since it started after cleaning, the most likely cause is simply moisture or residue preventing the spark module from resetting properly. Please switch off and unplug the hob, then lift each burner cap and crown to dry them thoroughly and wipe the white ceramic igniter tips clean before seating them flat again. Let me know if that stops the clicking."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok did that, unplugged it for the afternoon and its stopped clicking now. no gas smell. is it ok to use agen?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, it is perfectly safe to use your hob now as long as you are sure everything is dry. To prevent this from happening again, make sure the burner caps and igniters are completely dry before you put them back in place after cleaning. Please let me know if you need any further assistance or have other questions."
  }
 ],
